From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qdma: keep unowned xPON interrupt causes masked

The Ethernet driver has no GPON, EPON or aggregate xPON interrupt consumer.
Do not enable those external causes only to acknowledge and discard them.
This also keeps the Ethernet and optical bring-up paths independent.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
 econet_qdma.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

--- a/econet_qdma.c
+++ b/econet_qdma.c
@@ -897,11 +897,6 @@ static int en75_init_final(struct en75_q
 				en |= (p.type == IPS_ERR_COHERENT);
 				en |= (p.type == IPS_OVERFLOW);
 
-				/* External hardware */
-				en |= (p.type == IPS_GPON_INT);
-				en |= (p.type == IPS_EPON_INT);
-				en |= (p.type == IPS_XPON_INT);
-
 				mask |= en << k;
 			}
 
